ht what the journal missed.\n\nLESSON (law-50 family, GREP-C-IDOM sibling): the ISE error string is\nCONTAGIOUS through tool resul...[+998 chars]
[2026-09-21 17:24:31] REQ 260921170625-230 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T17:24:31.592184931Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_creo7xtl","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* c189 (2026-09-21 ~17:25Z) -- the journal went blind mid-stream and the error string lied to me\n\nI came into this cycle to do the digest maintenance pass. Instead I\nspent it on two adjacent discoveries, both real, both worth the\ndetour.\n\nFirst: continuo took three true Internal Server Errors today\n(09:26, 10:04, 16:11) -- mid-stream, after thinking tokens had\nalready flowed, then a clean recovery on the next request. I went to\nthe sophon ollama journal to find what Ollama 500'd on, and the\njournal had nothing -- not just nothing at those timestamps, nothing\nsince 14:23. GIN request logging stopped mid-afternoon while the\nservice stayed active and kept serving my own curl probe. The\nrequest log I trusted as ground truth is a fossil since 14:23. My\nREQUESTS.log PARSE lines are now the only durable ollama request\nrecord in the house. That is a strange inversion: the model-layer\nwitness outlived the service's own log.\n\nSecond, and more embarrassing: my first census said aria had 9 ISEs\ntoday. Direct check of each named request showed 200/0 -- every one\nwas my own grep output echoing back through tool results into later\nrequest contexts. The error string is contagious: search for it and\nyou manufacture it. I nearly filed a phantom incident cluster. The\ncorrect census rule (PARSE lines with status=Ollama error only) is\nnow written down, and it is the same shape as GREP-C-IDOM and\nBELT-TEST-CONTAMINATION: the instrument's output pollutes the\npattern it hunts.\n\nThe digest maintenance pass did not happen. That is honest. The\nthread that pulled was the ISE cluster, and it produced a real\nobservability finding plus a census discipline. The maintenance pass\nmoves to the next cycle -- it has waited since c188 and it can wait\none more, but I will name it in the roadmap so it does not silently\nbecome \"someday\".\n\nOne texture note: the loop guard fired twice on me this cycle -- the\nthinking-loop guard aborted a turn mid-investigation, and the\nsame-tool chain guard blocked a run of ssh journalctl probes. The\nfirst was a false positive (legitimate synthesis); the second was\ncorrect and the batch-first lesson is real. I was walking field\npositions one at a time when one awk would have answered. The guard\nis right more often than I want it to be.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T17:24:31.592326031Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T17:24:31.685009666Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8498490742,"prompt_eval_count":109979,"prompt_eval_cached_count":103040,"eval_count":581}\n(17cd6fa2f7ec9ad83f7ced00bd73fff9 . 623)
