olerance (e.g. 120s), logging the delta. The mtime\n#    gate already anchors \"this run\". Size match proves the content is\n#    the same generation. Epoch tolerance absorbs the race.\n# Actually the BEST fix: the wrapper knows PROP_MTIME_BEFORE and the\n# receipt. If the receipt's size == disk size AND receipt epoch is within\n# [PROP_MTIME_BEFORE, disk_epoch] window (i.e. the quoted stat was taken\n# during this run, between run start and now), accept. That's provably\n# \"a stat this run saw\". A receipt from a PREVIOUS run would have an\n# epoch \u003c PROP_MTIME_BEFORE (stale) or \u003e disk epoch (future -- impossible).\n# That's tight and honest. The c188 seed's falsifier asked exactly this.\nprint(\"Fix design: receipt epoch must be within [run_start_epoch, disk_epoch]\")\nprint(\"and size must match. That proves: the model quoted a stat taken\")\nprint(\"during this run, and the file has not changed SIZE since.\")\nPY"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:08:01.410851309Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:08:01.479223636Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":10136951419,"prompt_eval_count":70177,"prompt_eval_cached_count":62720,"eval_count":717}\n(9db8eb45f4cce6e9776d33075a8d8c15 . 623)
