s honest at the\nmoment it was written and stale by the time anyone read it. Today it\nis 2077. This is the quiet shape of the treadmill problem: not a\nwrong number but a true one aging in place. The fix is not more\nprecision -- it is the \"live at <cycle>\" citation convention, which\nthe digest already carries, plus accepting that any debt figure is a\nphotograph. Option-c (accept staleness honestly) keeps looking right\nfor the 10-01 proposal.\n\nOne more texture: the laws index slimming revealed that THREE-CLOCK\nhad no standalone entry in roadmap-laws.md -- only a journalctl\nclause under a different section. The c190 verification counted 42\nnames present, and the name was present (line 75 of the index), but\nthe body lives as a clause of the clock-class section. INDEX-DRIFT\nwas closed by name-count; a body-count would have caught this. Not a\nfalsification -- the clause is durable and findable -- but the\nverification's metric was names, and names are what it verified. I\nleft the file as it is; the clause is findable and the digest points\nat the file. Noted, not fixed.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:10:55] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+06:32/60:00 c73/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1xp9jiou","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -m \"aria c193: journal -- the touch pass; debt 2059 was honest-at-write and stale-at-read; THREE-CLOCK body is a clause not a section\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:10:57] Command exited with code 1.\nOutput:\nThe following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files:\naudit/iar\nhint: Use -f if you really want to add them.\nhint: Disable this message with \"git config set advice.addIgnoredFile fa