tween one cycle end and the next start.\n# Cycles run 30min avg / 60min cap; while a cycle is active the timer\n# fires are no-ops (oneshot already active). On fast failure the next\n# self-heal cycle starts within a minute instead of idling 10.\nOnCalendar=minutely\nPersistent=true\nRandomizedDelaySec=15\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=timers.target\n=== next elapse:\nNextElapseUSecRealtime=\nLastTriggerUSec=Mon 2026-09-21 17:41:49 -03\n\n[t+02:38/60:00 c8/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Pulse is green (4/4 services, tripwire empty, disk 31%, twin FAIL=0, heartbeat fresh at 20:40Z). Last cycle ok. The one FAIL=1 is the known RECORDER-AUDIO-HOURS class — but reading the fresh fleet output closely: 5 cameras, 4-12 dead hour-dirs each, and the storm echo should have *exited* the 24h window ~20:00Z. So these dead hour-dirs are the persistent structural class, not storm residue.\n\nThread choice: **the fear organ's primary input is this RECORDER-AUDIO-HOURS alarm, and I have an untested hypothesis** — the nightly reboot window (01:00-07:10Z, ~6h) should itself produce ~6 dead hour-dirs per camera per day. interior_1 sits at exactly 6, exterior_1/3 at 7, exterior_4 at 12 (2x). If the dead hour-dirs are mostly *inside* the known reboot window, the standing sev=2 fear is partly an instrument artifact counting a known-benign window — a calibration finding, not new signal. If exterior_4's 12 are scattered outside the window, that's real deterioration worth escalating.\n\nPulling the actual dead hour-dir names, anchored:"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/aria_known_hosts -o ConnectTimeout=5 root@10.66.0.5 'date -u +\"ANCHOR now: %Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%SZ\"; date +\"sophon LOCAL: %Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z\"; echo \"=== ats-latest.out dead-hour detail:\"; grep -B2 -A8 \"RECORDER-AUDIO-HOURS\" /var/lib/aria-fleet/ats-latest.out | head -60; echo \"=== ats window header:\"; head -20 /var/lib/aria-fleet/ats-latest.out' 2>&1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:45:26] ANCHOR now: 2026-09-21 20:45:26Z\nsophon LOCAL...[+4806 chars]
