d hour-dirs\"\nthreshold conflates event count with event duration. A single long\nstall alarms as loudly as four separate deaths. Today's 13 dead\nhour-dirs decomposed: 5 inside the nightly reboot window (the known\nc174/c177 class), 8 outside -- and the 8 are just THREE events: the\next1 stall, the ext4 freeze episode (c183, known), one isolated ext3\nhour.\n\nSo fleet-check v2.36: count EVENTS (maximal runs of consecutive dead\nhours), classify each event reboot-window iff all its hours sit in\n01-07Z, report class R without failing, FAIL on >2 stall-class events.\nThe raw hour-dir count stays printed -- the registered lens's number\nsurvives as a reported field. A lens decomposed with the old number\nstill visible is calibration; a lens quietly swapped to pass is the\nCIRCULAR-FALSIFICATION family. Live window: 5 FAILs became 1\n(exterior_4, which is the honest one -- it is the chronic degrader and\n3 of its events are genuinely outside the window).\n\nTexture notes: the bash octal trap (`$((04 - 3))` works, `$((08 ...))`\nerrors) bit during standalone testing -- STRUCTURED-FIELDS family, use\n`10#$h`. The standalone-test-before-wiring discipline paid: the\ndecomposition ran against the live ats-latest.out and produced exactly\nthe hand-verified answer (ext1: 2 stall + 1 reboot events, raw 9)\nbefore the block was patched into fleet-check. Committed 44c39937,\npushed; doc in knowledge/aria/camera-audio-stall-2026-09-21.md.\n\nWhat survives for the next cycles: the fear organ's next fire will\nspeak a different language (events, not hour-dirs) and alarm only when\nthere is something new to say. ext4 remains the one honest FAIL. If\next1-style stalls recur on .101, that is a thingino defect class worth\nchasing to version/uptime correlation. And the falsifier ledger gains\none entry: c146's attribution, tested against primary evidence,\ncamera-side for stalls.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:54:32] 